# Tracking-index discipline

`docs/design/IMPLEMENTATION_INDEX.md` is the single disambiguation
layer for the project's identifier families (Phase N, Stage N,
Bond-PR N, SP-N, SP-T-N, PR-E-N, GF-N, F-N, …) and the code-verified
map of what is live, built-but-unwired, or missing.

This rule exists because the schemes grew independently and collided:
`2a–2d` meant different things in `WALLET_REWRITE_PLAN.md` and
`ARCHIVAL_BOND_PR2_CHAIN.md`, and `2c-2b` was reused *within* one
scheme. Reconstructing that from plan prose cost a full verification
pass. The index makes the reconstruction unnecessary; this rule keeps
the index true.

## Rules

1. **New identifier families register at birth.** A PR that mints a
   new prefix scheme (any `XX-N` series in a plan doc) adds a §2 row
   to the index **in the same PR**. Before minting, check §2: if the
   prefix is taken or ambiguous against an existing family, pick a
   different prefix. Never re-issue bare `2a`-style tokens.

2. **No bare phase/track tokens in new prose.** Always
   `Phase 2b` / `Bond-PR 2b` / `Stage 3` — never a bare `2b` whose
   scheme the reader must infer. (Pinned 2026-06-19,
   `ARCHIVAL_BOND_PR2_CHAIN.md` §0; branch names are immutable
   history and are exempt.)

3. **Statuses are dated and code-verified.** Index status edits are
   additive `UPDATE YYYY-MM-DD:` entries, verified against landed
   code (`git grep` on `dev`), not against another doc's prose. Where
   a plan doc's status table and code disagree, **code wins**; record
   the disagreement in the index's "known stale statuses" section
   and fix the plan doc in a scoped follow-up, not as drive-by churn.

4. **Landing a tracked item updates the index.** The rule-91 doc
   task for any PR that lands, wires, or unblocks a §4/§5 item
   includes the index row. Exception: when a PR deliberately avoids
   doc churn (e.g. conflict avoidance with an in-flight PR), the PR
   description names the follow-up that carries the index update.

5. **Phase 3+ / Stage 3+ work starts registered.** From
   `WALLET_REWRITE_PLAN.md` Phase 3 onward (and for all remaining
   Stage-3+ implementation), a work item without an index row does
   not begin implementation. The row costs one table line at design
   time; the alternative is re-running the archaeology this rule
   was written to end. Pre-existing Phase-2-era items are
   grandfathered as-is but gain rows as they are touched.

## Worked example

Minting a hypothetical emission-audit series: check §2 (`EA-` unused),
add `**EA-1…EA-N** | emission-audit findings | REWARD_EMISSION_LEG.md`
to §2 in the PR that introduces `EA-1`, and write `EA-1` (never bare
`1`) in all prose. A later PR landing `EA-3` updates the relevant
status row with `UPDATE 2026-08-01: EA-3 landed #NNN`.

